ld: do not add GNU tooldir library paths on Peios

Peios has one architecture-specific runtime library directory:
/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-peios.  The native linker's generic tooldir fallback
adds /usr/x86_64-linux-peios/lib64 and /usr/x86_64-linux-peios/lib even when
--with-lib-path supplies the distribution path.  Neither tooldir exists in
the Peios filesystem layout, so compiling them into every linker script is
both misleading and wasted lookup work.

Keep the normal GNU behaviour for every upstream target and suppress the
fallback only for the Peios target.  The explicit --with-lib-path remains
the sole SEARCH_DIR.

diff -ur a/ld/genscripts.sh b/ld/genscripts.sh
--- a/ld/genscripts.sh
+++ b/ld/genscripts.sh
@@ -248,6 +248,7 @@
 # Always search $(tooldir)/lib, aka /usr/local/TARGET/lib when native
 # except when LIB_PATH=":".
-if [ "${LIB_PATH}" != ":" ] ; then
+# Peios has no tooldir library tree; --with-lib-path is authoritative there.
+if [ "${LIB_PATH}" != ":" ] && [ "${target##*-}" != peios ] ; then
   libs=
   if [ "x${TOOL_LIB}" = "x" ] ; then
     if [ "x${NATIVE}" = "xyes" ] ; then
